    "text": "9 hours ago Remember when dinner showed up on a tray hooked to your car window? In a handful of Ohio towns, that still happens every single day. Carhops walk out to your car, take your order, and bring burgers, fries, and root beer floats right to your seat. Plenty of drive-ins have faded away over the years, but these six are still serving it the old way. Read full article\n7",
